class AutoModeActivityJudgeScope(StrEnum):
    """
    JudgeScope says which commands reach the judge. It is one selector rather
    than a set of booleans so that no two modes can be in force at once.

     - JUDGE_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED: Judge nothing. The policy still supplies deployment_context to the
    cmd_line policies that carry the AUTO action and judge on their own.

    This is also what an endorctl too old to know a value added later reads,
    so every future value fails safe.
     - JUDGE_SCOPE_MATCHED_COMMANDS: Judge the commands a RISK command policy already matched, treating the
    action of each matched policy as AUTO.

    This overrides an explicit customer decision in BOTH directions: a policy
    that says block stops blocking and asks the judge, and one that says alert
    or feedback can escalate to a block on a suspicious label. The override
    lasts only as long as the judge answers — with no label each policy keeps
    its own action, so an outage degrades to the enforcement the tenant had.
    A GOVERNANCE policy is never overridden, and a command that only a
    governance policy matched is not judged at all.
     - JUDGE_SCOPE_ALL_COMMANDS: Judge every command and stand the RISK command policies down. The malware
    and secrets checks are untouched: they carry real detections rather than
    regular expressions.

    The patterns are still evaluated. They are stood down by a label coming
    back rather than by this scope alone, which is what lets a judge that
    cannot be reached fall back to the verdict they produced.

    An allowlist stands down on the same terms as a blocklist, so a command
    absent from the set a tenant permitted runs anyway if the judge finds
    nothing wrong with it. Mark a command policy GOVERNANCE to keep its
    action final: a governance match keeps its own action under every label.
    The judge still rules on the command itself, so a review or suspicious
    label also raises an ask or a block against the auto-mode policy, next to
    the governance match.
    """

    JUDGE_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED = 'JUDGE_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED'
    JUDGE_SCOPE_MATCHED_COMMANDS = 'JUDGE_SCOPE_MATCHED_COMMANDS'
    JUDGE_SCOPE_ALL_COMMANDS = 'JUDGE_SCOPE_ALL_COMMANDS'


